import re

# Returns a Match object if the entire string matches the gauge pattern
re.fullmatch(r"PE-\d{4}", "PE-0137")

# Returns a list of all decimal numbers in the line
re.findall(r"\d+\.\d+", line)

# Splits the line by commas and any surrounding whitespace
re.split(r"\s*,\s*", line)

# Squeezes multiple whitespace characters into a single space
re.sub(r"\s+", " ", line)
Escaping Dots (\. vs .)
​Unescaped . matches any character except a newline.  
​Escaped \. matches a literal dot. Forgetting to escape dots allows invalid inputs with arbitrary characters to pass through.  
​4. Key Takeaways & Practical Application
​Read Patterns Out Loud: Deconstruct and read short regex patterns token-by-token in plain English.  
​Regex vs. Split: While split() is useful for standard structured data, re.findall() handles messy inputs with varying spacing, missing separators, or stray tabs much more robustly.  
​Anchor Validation: Always apply anchors when validating fixed-format codes or full strings (e.g., product IDs or phone numbers).  
